{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Deep Q-Networks (DQN) Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code here is stdlib-only numpy-free \u2014 we use a hand-rolled single-hidden-layer MLP on a tiny continuous GridWorld, so every training step runs in microseconds. The algorithm is identical to Atari DQN at scale."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: replay buffer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ReplayBuffer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, capacity):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.buf = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.capacity = capacity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def push(self, s, a, r, s_next, done):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if len(self.buf) == self.capacity:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.buf.pop(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.buf.append((s, a, r, s_next, done))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def sample(self, batch, rng):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return rng.sample(self.buf, batch)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "~50,000 capacity for Atari; 5,000 suffices for our toy env."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: a tiny Q-network (manual MLP)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class QNet:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_in, n_hidden, n_actions, rng):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.W1 = [[rng.gauss(0, 0.3) for _ in range(n_in)] for _ in range(n_hidden)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b1 = [0.0] * n_hidden"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.W2 = [[rng.gauss(0, 0.3) for _ in range(n_hidden)] for _ in range(n_actions)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.b2 = [0.0] * n_actions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h = [max(0.0, sum(w * xi for w, xi in zip(row, x)) + b) for row, b in zip(self.W1, self.b1)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        q = [sum(w * hi for w, hi in zip(row, h)) + b for row, b in zip(self.W2, self.b2)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return q, h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Forward pass: linear \u2192 ReLU \u2192 linear. That is the entire net."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: the DQN update"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_step(online, target, batch, gamma, lr):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grads = zeros_like(online)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for s, a, r, s_next, done in batch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        q, h = online.forward(s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if done:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            y = r"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            q_next, _ = target.forward(s_next)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            y = r + gamma * max(q_next)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        td_error = q[a] - y"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        accumulate_grads(grads, online, s, h, a, td_error)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    apply_sgd(online, grads, lr / len(batch))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The shape is Q-learning from Lesson 04 with two differences: (a) we backprop through a differentiable `Q(\u00b7; \u03b8)` instead of indexing a table, (b) the target uses `Q(\u00b7; \u03b8^-)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: the outer loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For each episode, act \u03b5-greedy on `Q(\u00b7; \u03b8)`, push transitions into the buffer, sample a minibatch, take a gradient step, periodically sync `\u03b8^- \u2190 \u03b8`. The pattern:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for episode in range(N):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = env.reset()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while not done:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a = epsilon_greedy(online, s, epsilon)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s_next, r, done = env.step(s, a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        buffer.push(s, a, r, s_next, done)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if len(buffer) >= batch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            train_step(online, target, buffer.sample(batch), gamma, lr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if steps % sync_every == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            target = copy(online)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s = s_next"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "On our tiny GridWorld with a 16-dim one-hot state, the agent learns a near-optimal policy in ~500 episodes. On Atari, scale this to 200M frames and add a CNN feature extractor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Plot the per-episode return curve. How many episodes until the running mean exceeds -10?\n2. **Medium.** Disable the target network (use the online net for both sides of the Bellman target). Measure training instability \u2014 does return oscillate or diverge?\n3. **Hard.** Add Double DQN: use the online net to pick `argmax a'`, target net to evaluate. Compare bias of `Q(s_0, best_a)` vs true `V*(s_0)` after 1,000 episodes with vs without Double DQN on a noisy-reward GridWorld."
      ]
    }
